WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:04.339
There's a lot of cool trivia out there about
Darth Vader, the most legendary villain in

00:00:04.339 --> 00:00:05.720
the Star Wars universe.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.850
Did you know it took five separate actors
to bring Luke's father to life in the original

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:10.850
flicks?

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:15.200
Or that James Earl Jones wasn't credited as
the voice of Vader until Return of the Jedi?

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.190
That kind of knowledge might help you win
a pub quiz, but it's just scratching the surface.

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:20.680
Let's talk about some deep cuts.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:25.190
Here are some facts about the Sith lord only
true Vader nerds know...

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:27.160
Darth Ubiquitous

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:32.640
Vader is the only human character to appear
in every main Star Wars feature film in some

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.120
way, shape, or form.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:37.820
Not Han, not Leia, not Luke ... not Porkins,
unfortunately …

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:42.130
… only the half-human, cyborg Darth Vader
can claim that title.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.610
"You are beaten!

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.570
It is useless to resist."

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:49.960
Obviously, Vader's villainy was central to
the original trilogy, and his origin story

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:52.649
formed the entire backbone of prequels.

00:00:52.649 --> 00:00:57.140
But thirty years after Darth Vader's death
within the Star Wars universe, he remains

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:02.079
so important that he even showed up in episode
seven … or at least his mangled helmet did

00:01:02.079 --> 00:01:08.060
… and he also made a stunning appearance
in 2016's Rogue One, which brings us to ...

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.180
Darth Expeditious

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:14.190
Although the Sith Lord's appearance onscreen
midway through Rogue One was written into

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:19.140
the script from the get-go, his most incredible
scene came at the very end, and foreshadowed

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:24.200
Vader's reign of terror in the original trilogy
to come: an intense hallway battle sequence

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:28.920
in which a besieged ship full of rebels raced
to escape with their stolen blueprints for

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:29.920
the Death Star.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:34.990
All while Vader advanced on them, lightsaber
in hand, cutting down every last man with

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:36.630
casual brutality.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:40.530
It's an incredible moment, made that much
more remarkable because it was tacked on at

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:45.600
the last possible moment after Rogue One's
editor argued Vader needed more screentime.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:49.810
Director Gareth Edwards said editor Jabez
Olssen thought one more badass moment was

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:50.869
called for.

00:01:50.869 --> 00:01:54.750
But Olssen's timing was awful: the film was
about four months from release.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:59.040
Ultimately, the sequence was shot in three
days — an incredible feat, considering it

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:03.619
ended up being among the best and most memorable
scenes in the entire film.

00:02:03.619 --> 00:02:05.340
Darth Repetitious

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:10.629
Vader was downright terrifying in Rogue One,
but if you look closely at his deadly stroll

00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:14.590
down that hallway, you'll realize you've seen
all of these moves before.

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:16.430
They didn't teach an old dog new tricks …

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:17.430
"Ah!

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:19.730
Thy will be done, Lord Vader."

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:25.069
He deflects laser blasts … uses the force
to lift and choke … as well as disarm … and

00:02:25.069 --> 00:02:28.829
there's of course the lightsaber hacking and
slashing we all know and love.

00:02:28.829 --> 00:02:33.000
While it may have been tempting to give the
old-school Vader a new trick or two, according

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.959
to director Gareth Edwards, keeping his deadly
skill set familiar was "the golden rule" ...

00:02:37.959 --> 00:02:41.909
"Everything you sort of see him doing down
that corridor is pretty much something from

00:02:41.909 --> 00:02:43.159
the previous films."

00:02:43.159 --> 00:02:47.930
… which is why Vader wasn't breakdance fighting
or shooting fireballs from his hands.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:48.930
Good call.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:50.109
Darth Minimus

00:02:50.109 --> 00:02:54.989
Forget that handless farmboy Luke Skywalker:
Vader's the real star of the series, having

00:02:54.989 --> 00:02:58.049
left his mark on every episode and then some.

00:02:58.049 --> 00:03:03.459
But did you know that the franchise's fallen
hero, the most iconic villain in all of sci-fi,

00:03:03.459 --> 00:03:06.019
was in the first movie for fewer than ten
minutes.

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:07.019
Ten minutes!

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:10.389
That's like half a Fresh Prince episode, without
the commercials …

00:03:10.389 --> 00:03:15.739
"Ochina one little fight in a waslano scared
and witninnie witnnoone auntie and uncle in

00:03:15.739 --> 00:03:16.739
Bel-Air."

00:03:16.739 --> 00:03:20.909
It feels like he's in the film for much longer,
which is a testament to how effective those

00:03:20.909 --> 00:03:24.860
ten minutes were in introducing such an enigmatic
and menacing character.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:29.629
Compare that to the insufferable seventeen
minutes plus we had to spend with Jar Jar

00:03:29.629 --> 00:03:34.010
Binks in Episode One .. it's enough to make
you want to Force Choke yourself to death...

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:35.079
Thanks for watching!

00:03:35.079 --> 00:03:37.639
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:03:37.639 --> 00:03:39.439
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

